s ::= import "./schema.zt";
h ::= import "./helpers.zt";

area :: s.Area = (h.area "zenoh-service-client" "Zenoh service client protocol, wire records and holder adapter" {
    "components/lib/src/zenoh_service_client.rs";
    "components/proto/src/zenoh_service_client*.rs";
    "components/applications/zenoh-holder-*/**";
    "contracts/zenoh-service-client/**";
  } {
    -- legacy 01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea (done): Fix the Zenoh service client protocol
    -- A local holder has no way to speak to the Zenoh service. No contract says what a request names, what
    -- a completion reports, or what a take returns. Four rules are undecided. A request names a grant row
    -- by its index and never a key, because a key string in a request grants nothing. The service learns
    -- the holder from the endpoint the request arrives on, so no field names a holder. A request and a
    -- completion must fit the IO0 payloads of 56 and 24 bytes. A sample header and its payload must fit
    -- the data page. This item fixes those rules as a Zutai schema and judges it before any client library
    -- or component exists.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-439775fbf881"
      "The schema states format version 1 and the magic for `ZSVC`, as a little-endian integer. It states four queue slots, one ring page and one data page of 4096 bytes each. A success status is zero."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 24; } "The checker counts 24 facts that the judge derives from the schema text. They are constants, layouts, IO0 fit, signs, the row index, the data page, distinct values, flags and a served holder. The count is exact. The judge reads no Rust, so these facts come from the schema and the two contracts it is checked against.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-4398ab605484"
      "The request, completion, sample header and loan layouts add up to 32, 24, 16 and 64 bytes. Each layout equals a field list that the judge holds apart from the schema. Each layout lists the fields of its record type in order. Every record field has the type `Int`. A commented field is not a field."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 24; } "The checker counts 24 facts that the judge derives from the schema text. They are constants, layouts, IO0 fit, signs, the row index, the data page, distinct values, flags and a served holder. The count is exact. The judge reads no Rust, so these facts come from the schema and the two contracts it is checked against.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-4399566d5a7c"
      "A request of 32 bytes is within the IO0 request payload of 56. A completion of 24 bytes is within the IO0 completion payload of 24."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 24; } "The checker counts 24 facts that the judge derives from the schema text. They are constants, layouts, IO0 fit, signs, the row index, the data page, distinct values, flags and a served holder. The count is exact. The judge reads no Rust, so these facts come from the schema and the two contracts it is checked against.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-439acfbcdb33"
      "No field name contains key, holder, session, peer, link, topic or name. A request names a grant row by its index."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 24; } "The checker counts 24 facts that the judge derives from the schema text. They are constants, layouts, IO0 fit, signs, the row index, the data page, distinct values, flags and a served holder. The count is exact. The judge reads no Rust, so these facts come from the schema and the two contracts it is checked against.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-439b7772ab05"
      "The sequence, the timestamp and the status are signed. A reserved field is an unsigned byte array and a named field is not a byte array."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 24; } "The checker counts 24 facts that the judge derives from the schema text. They are constants, layouts, IO0 fit, signs, the row index, the data page, distinct values, flags and a served holder. The count is exact. The judge reads no Rust, so these facts come from the schema and the two contracts it is checked against.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-439c11340981"
      "The request and the completion carry the row in two bytes, and `maxRows` is 65535."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 24; } "The checker counts 24 facts that the judge derives from the schema text. They are constants, layouts, IO0 fit, signs, the row index, the data page, distinct values, flags and a served holder. The count is exact. The judge reads no Rust, so these facts come from the schema and the two contracts it is checked against.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-439d8f810a6e"
      "The sample header of 16 bytes and the largest payload of 4080 bytes fill the data page of 4096 bytes. The largest payload is at most the grants contract's sample limit."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 24; } "The checker counts 24 facts that the judge derives from the schema text. They are constants, layouts, IO0 fit, signs, the row index, the data page, distinct values, flags and a served holder. The count is exact. The judge reads no Rust, so these facts come from the schema and the two contracts it is checked against.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-439e556cc092"
      "The five operations, the six statuses, the three items and the two loan roles are distinct within their group. Operations are positive and failures are negative. The item none is zero. Each value fits the width and sign of the field that carries it."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 24; } "The checker counts 24 facts that the judge derives from the schema text. They are constants, layouts, IO0 fit, signs, the row index, the data page, distinct values, flags and a served holder. The count is exact. The judge reads no Rust, so these facts come from the schema and the two contracts it is checked against.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-439f84a63f01"
      "The known completion flags equal the sum of the flags, and each flag is one bit."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 24; } "The checker counts 24 facts that the judge derives from the schema text. They are constants, layouts, IO0 fit, signs, the row index, the data page, distinct values, flags and a served holder. The count is exact. The judge reads no Rust, so these facts come from the schema and the two contracts it is checked against.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-43a09ca14007"
      "A holder with five rows and samples of 12 bytes is served by this protocol. A sample of 4081 bytes, a sample of no bytes, a holder of no rows and a holder of 65536 rows are each refused."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 24; } "The checker counts 24 facts that the judge derives from the schema text. They are constants, layouts, IO0 fit, signs, the row index, the data page, distinct values, flags and a served holder. The count is exact. The judge reads no Rust, so these facts come from the schema and the two contracts it is checked against.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-43a1b1c9751b"
      "The committed Rust constants file equals the generator's output byte for byte. Ten edits are each refused. They change a value, drop or add a constant, swap two, or change a type. They also drop the header, append a comment, use CRLF, drop the final newline or empty the file."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 24; } "The checker counts 24 facts that the judge derives from the schema text. They are constants, layouts, IO0 fit, signs, the row index, the data page, distinct values, flags and a served holder. The count is exact. The judge reads no Rust, so these facts come from the schema and the two contracts it is checked against.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-43a2dbfaf50d"
      "The judge refuses 80 corruptions before it checks the generated file. They are 66 edits of the schema, 4 holders that the protocol cannot serve and 10 edits of the generated file."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_client_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 80; } "The checker refuses exactly 80 corruptions before it checks the generated file. They are 66 edits of the schema, 4 holders the protocol cannot serve and 10 edits of the generated file. A dropped or invented control changes the count and re-admits the item.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad60-751f-81b8-43a304becda4"
      "`just zenoh_service_client_check` exits zero and reports its observations through the gate adapter."
      "Fix the Zenoh service client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "recipe-passed" "zenoh_service_client_check" h.noPredicates "The gate adapter reports the recipe's exit code, so the checker cannot vouch for itself. The recipe fails until the generated constants file lands.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-fa21-739d-a55e-ef59fa3ce0ea"; }; };
    -- legacy 01a18328-71de-7291-922f-87adc0b3a8cc (done): Generate and judge the Zenoh service client wire records
    -- The Zenoh service client protocol has constants and layouts and no encoder or decoder. A holder and
    -- the service would each write the field offsets by hand. A hand-written offset for a format that
    -- crosses a process boundary is what the repository forbids. Four rules are undecided in code. Each
    -- record must encode to the bytes the schema's layout gives. Each record must decode back to the value
    -- it was encoded from. A buffer shorter than the record must be refused. A signed field must stay
    -- signed and a multi-byte field must be little-endian. This item generates the encoders and decoders
    -- from the layouts and judges them before any client or service uses them.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ada1-7700-83f1-0e85eccbd9bc"
      "The generator renders a struct, an encoder and a decoder for the request, the completion, the sample header and the loan descriptor. Their lengths are 32, 24, 16 and 64 bytes."
      "Generate and judge the Zenoh service client wire records"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_wire_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 17; } "The checker counts 13 lines that the Rust test printed. They are four sizes, four encodings, four round trips and one verdict. It also counts 4 refusals of a short buffer. The total is 17. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the client schema's judge passes.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-71de-7291-922f-87adc0b3a8cc"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ada1-7700-83f1-0e86b1c13724"
      "The committed Rust file equals the renderer's output byte for byte. Eleven edits are each refused. They move an offset, change a field type or an endianness, drop a length check or an encoded field, or remove the header. They also append a comment, use CRLF, drop the final newline or empty the file."
      "Generate and judge the Zenoh service client wire records"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_client_wire_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 76; } "The checker refuses exactly 76 corruptions before it runs any Rust. They are 40 transcripts, 11 edits of the generated file, 7 corrupted layouts and 18 corrupted exports. A dropped or invented control changes the count and re-admits the item.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-71de-7291-922f-87adc0b3a8cc"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ada1-7700-83f1-0e87f9d593ed"
      "The bytes the Rust encoder prints for each record equal what Python's `struct` writes from the schema's layout. Every field, reserved padding included, holds a distinct nonzero pattern."
      "Generate and judge the Zenoh service client wire records"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_wire_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 17; } "The checker counts 13 lines that the Rust test printed. They are four sizes, four encodings, four round trips and one verdict. It also counts 4 refusals of a short buffer. The total is 17. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the client schema's judge passes.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-71de-7291-922f-87adc0b3a8cc"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ada1-7700-83f1-0e88634d387f"
      "Each record decodes to the value it was encoded from."
      "Generate and judge the Zenoh service client wire records"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_wire_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 17; } "The checker counts 13 lines that the Rust test printed. They are four sizes, four encodings, four round trips and one verdict. It also counts 4 refusals of a short buffer. The total is 17. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the client schema's judge passes.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-71de-7291-922f-87adc0b3a8cc"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ada1-7700-83f1-0e898ffd74ff"
      "A buffer one byte shorter than the record is refused for each of the four records. A longer buffer is read from its start."
      "Generate and judge the Zenoh service client wire records"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_wire_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 17; } "The checker counts 13 lines that the Rust test printed. They are four sizes, four encodings, four round trips and one verdict. It also counts 4 refusals of a short buffer. The total is 17. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the client schema's judge passes.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-71de-7291-922f-87adc0b3a8cc"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ada1-7700-83f1-0e8ae1233a9c"
      "The request sequence, the sample timestamp and the completion status are signed and little-endian. The test encodes a negative value in each."
      "Generate and judge the Zenoh service client wire records"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_wire_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 17; } "The checker counts 13 lines that the Rust test printed. They are four sizes, four encodings, four round trips and one verdict. It also counts 4 refusals of a short buffer. The total is 17. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the client schema's judge passes.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-71de-7291-922f-87adc0b3a8cc"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ada1-7700-83f1-0e8bd0113c8d"
      "The judge reads the layouts from the schema. Seven corrupted layouts each make the honest transcript fail. They narrow a field, change a sign, swap two fields or widen the padding."
      "Generate and judge the Zenoh service client wire records"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_client_wire_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 76; } "The checker refuses exactly 76 corruptions before it runs any Rust. They are 40 transcripts, 11 edits of the generated file, 7 corrupted layouts and 18 corrupted exports. A dropped or invented control changes the count and re-admits the item.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-71de-7291-922f-87adc0b3a8cc"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ada1-7700-83f1-0e8cee58231b"
      "`components/proto/src/lib.rs` holds the export of the wire records once, with no attribute directly above it. The Rust test imports the records through the crate and includes no source by path. Eighteen corrupted files are each refused. They remove or comment out the export or wrap it in a block comment or an inline module. They also put an attribute above it, indent it, make it private, rename it or double it. For the test, they remove the import or include the generated file by path."
      "Generate and judge the Zenoh service client wire records"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_wire_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 17; } "The checker counts 13 lines that the Rust test printed. They are four sizes, four encodings, four round trips and one verdict. It also counts 4 refusals of a short buffer. The total is 17. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the client schema's judge passes.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-71de-7291-922f-87adc0b3a8cc"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ada1-7700-83f1-0e8dc0a2a588"
      "The slice runs the client schema's judge and requires its 24 facts and 80 controls first."
      "Generate and judge the Zenoh service client wire records"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_wire_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 17; } "The checker counts 13 lines that the Rust test printed. They are four sizes, four encodings, four round trips and one verdict. It also counts 4 refusals of a short buffer. The total is 17. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the client schema's judge passes.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-71de-7291-922f-87adc0b3a8cc"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ada1-7700-83f1-0e8e9ca176ab"
      "The judge refuses 76 corruptions before it runs any Rust. They are 40 transcripts, 11 generated files, 7 layouts and 18 corrupted exports."
      "Generate and judge the Zenoh service client wire records"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_client_wire_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 76; } "The checker refuses exactly 76 corruptions before it runs any Rust. They are 40 transcripts, 11 edits of the generated file, 7 corrupted layouts and 18 corrupted exports. A dropped or invented control changes the count and re-admits the item.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-71de-7291-922f-87adc0b3a8cc"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ada1-7700-83f1-0e8f53178c55"
      "`just zenoh_service_client_wire_check` exits zero and reports its observations through the gate adapter."
      "Generate and judge the Zenoh service client wire records"
      {
        h.observedWhere "recipe-passed" "zenoh_service_client_wire_check" h.noPredicates "The gate adapter reports the recipe's exit code, so the checker cannot vouch for itself. The recipe fails until the generated file lands.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-71de-7291-922f-87adc0b3a8cc"; }; };
    -- legacy 01a18328-7a0d-7507-9850-cbbb0baae9ca (done): Write and judge the Zenoh service client adapter
    -- A local holder has no way to publish to or take from the Zenoh service. No code opens the session,
    -- bounds a request, checks an answer or returns a loan. Five rules are undecided in code. The adapter
    -- must refuse a request outside the protocol before it publishes anything. It must check every answer
    -- against the request it sent. It must poison the session and return both loans when an answer is
    -- missing or outside the protocol. It must return every loan it imported, whatever failed. It must not
    -- claim a clean detach after the session was poisoned. This item writes the adapter and judges it
    -- against a scripted service on the host, before any service component exists.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adaf-7404-bafb-35cb37661c13"
      "Attach sends the attach request and takes the ring loan and then the data loan. The service reports three rows and the adapter imports two loans. The attach request is the 32 bytes that the schema's layout gives."
      "Write and judge the Zenoh service client adapter"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_io_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 73; } "The checker counts 31 lines that the Rust test printed. They are loan checks, requests, slices, statuses, samples and teardowns. It also counts 42 refusals by name and class. The total is 73. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the schema's judge and the wire records' judge pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-7a0d-7507-9850-cbbb0baae9ca"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adaf-7404-bafb-35ccc6ad54e8"
      "Attach refuses ten cases after the service answered. They are data before ring, one buffer for both, one lease for both, no rows and too many rows. The others are a refused attach, no attach answer, a data loan that never arrives, no loans, and a ring the service did not format. Each returns exactly the loans it imported, and the data loan that never arrives returns the one ring loan."
      "Write and judge the Zenoh service client adapter"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_io_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 73; } "The checker counts 31 lines that the Rust test printed. They are loan checks, requests, slices, statuses, samples and teardowns. It also counts 42 refusals by name and class. The total is 73. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the schema's judge and the wire records' judge pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-7a0d-7507-9850-cbbb0baae9ca"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adaf-7404-bafb-35cd334539ad"
      "Attach refuses six cases before it sends anything. They are one endpoint for both and an unaligned ring base. The others are an unaligned data base, the same base twice, a zero base and a base that wraps."
      "Write and judge the Zenoh service client adapter"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_io_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 73; } "The checker counts 31 lines that the Rust test printed. They are loan checks, requests, slices, statuses, samples and teardowns. It also counts 42 refusals by name and class. The total is 73. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the schema's judge and the wire records' judge pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-7a0d-7507-9850-cbbb0baae9ca"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adaf-7404-bafb-35ce998f73fa"
      "A loan descriptor is valid with its magic, version, role, zero reserved bytes, the length of its role and nonzero identities. Eight corruptions of one field are each refused, and a data descriptor is valid only as a data loan."
      "Write and judge the Zenoh service client adapter"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_io_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 73; } "The checker counts 31 lines that the Rust test printed. They are loan checks, requests, slices, statuses, samples and teardowns. It also counts 42 refusals by name and class. The total is 73. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the schema's judge and the wire records' judge pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-7a0d-7507-9850-cbbb0baae9ca"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adaf-7404-bafb-35cfd4c32785"
      "A publication of three bytes on row 2 with sequence -7 writes the 32-byte request that the layout gives. It names the data page by its buffer and lease and reads three bytes from it. It reports two holders reached and a copy sent to the peer."
      "Write and judge the Zenoh service client adapter"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_io_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 73; } "The checker counts 31 lines that the Rust test printed. They are loan checks, requests, slices, statuses, samples and teardowns. It also counts 42 refusals by name and class. The total is 73. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the schema's judge and the wire records' judge pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-7a0d-7507-9850-cbbb0baae9ca"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adaf-7404-bafb-35d02894af01"
      "A take returns a sample from row 1 with its sequence, timestamp and four payload bytes, a loss of 16 and an empty ring. It asks the data page for the header and the buffer, naming the data page by its buffer and lease. A buffer of exactly 4080 bytes is accepted."
      "Write and judge the Zenoh service client adapter"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_io_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 73; } "The checker counts 31 lines that the Rust test printed. They are loan checks, requests, slices, statuses, samples and teardowns. It also counts 42 refusals by name and class. The total is 73. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the schema's judge and the wire records' judge pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-7a0d-7507-9850-cbbb0baae9ca"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adaf-7404-bafb-35d14caa34e0"
      "A row past the holder's rows, a payload past 4080 bytes and a take buffer past 4080 bytes are each refused as a bad request. Nothing is published, and the ring holds only the one request that was valid."
      "Write and judge the Zenoh service client adapter"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_client_io_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 73; } "The checker counts 31 lines that the Rust test printed. They are loan checks, requests, slices, statuses, samples and teardowns. It also counts 42 refusals by name and class. The total is 73. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the schema's judge and the wire records' judge pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a18328-7a0d-7507-9850-cbbb0baae9ca"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adaf-7404-bafb-35d2643374bb"
      "A denied publication, a publication on a closed link and an accepted one return statuses -1, -5 and 0. The session stays usable and no loan is returned."
      "Write and judge the Zenoh service client adapter"
      {
