      }) with { supersedes = { "01a186d0-03db-7232-a90f-70f0750a5793"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adbd-759e-bfba-a0132f9ced13"
      "The judge refuses 199 corruptions before it runs any Rust. They are 6 whole-transcript edits, 9 missing lines, 170 single-field changes, 11 wrong adapters and 3 corrupted request layouts. The judge fails if two controls corrupt a transcript the same way, so each of the 199 is distinct."
      "Judge the Zenoh service client adapter failed-attach abort"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_client_abort_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 199; } "The checker refuses exactly 199 corruptions before it runs any Rust. Every field of every line is changed alone, so a judge that stopped comparing one field fails. Eleven wrong adapters are written by name. One sends the abort before the attach answer is read. One returns a loan twice while the other leaks. One imports a slot on a refused attach and never returns it. Each corrupted layout is run through the judge with the honest transcript.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a186d0-03db-7232-a90f-70f0750a5793"; }; };
